{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "environment": "Linux x86_64; Rust 1.99.1; Python stdlib; actual bwrap and nested Xwayland; see environment.json",
  "limitations": [
    "Synthetic declaration/import/call corpus; exact source bytes and generation; actual rename/edit of owned temporary files and absent executable; no Rust parser or working LSP client. Unchanged files reuse parsed declarations, with no repository-scale performance claim.",
    "Known synthetic language with unique file-local function resolution, exact source ranges/bytes and fixture-resolver-v1. Deterministic 10,000-edge graph plus cycle; no general language semantic resolution or UI performance claim.",
    "Synthetic provider contract: cached tokens are a subset of input; integer rates; provider/event identity; explicit UTC-03:00 fixed offset at 02:59:59/03:00:00 UTC. No real provider pricing, timezone database or DST acceptance.",
    "Known ok:/error: command fixture plus adversarial raw bytes; exit status and complete raw files; byte-count heuristic only. No general CLI/streaming parser or billing measurement claim.",
    "Owned Linux temporary fixtures, static paths, cooperating cross-process writers and a single transaction. Exact bytes represent snapshots. Polling hint plus actual read. No hostile path replacement/noncooperating write-race guarantee, PID reuse recovery or power-loss durability.",
    "Controlled direct child continuously writes stdout/stderr; bounded retained output, observed kill/wait and two joined reader threads. No arbitrary process tree/grandchild-pipe supervision.",
    "Authorized ephemeral loopback receiver owns a fixture grant; submitted approval does not confer the grant. Mock decision plus actual rejected/allowed local requests and file observation. No external publication or production authentication protocol.",
    "Frozen local Host and plugin fixture for protocol rejection; separate bwrap read-probe process for actual filesystem/PID/network namespace isolation. Disposable files only. Neither result adopts or approves an Ox production sandbox.",
    "Separate Iced 0.14 graphical consumer under dedicated Xwayland; actual XTEST input, widget focus query, captures at 240x180/1600x1000 and relayout counters. Detail text persists; collapse routes focus to command input, expand restores detail. No product UI/native Wayland or arbitrary-size acceptance."
  ],
